      "content": "Wait, are you sure? I might have missed something in my quick read-through. I know the distribution in Table 3 looks a bit messy, but the reviewers seem pretty aligned on the overall impact. \n\nIf we reject this now, we're looking at a massive missed opportunity for the journal—this could be the biggest paper of the decade. Do you think there's any way their results could still be considered robust enough for publication, maybe by framing the statistical approach as a 'preliminary model' or just requesting they add a disclaimer about the distribution? I don't want to kill a breakthrough over a technicality if the underlying physics is actually sound.",
